Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ============================================================================
;  Fix: Microsoft Edge "Virus scan failed" when downloading files/templates
;  from the Saudization app.
;
;  Cause: the app is served over plain HTTP by IP/hostname, so Windows puts it
;  in the INTERNET zone. Every download then gets a "Mark of the Web" and Edge
;  asks the local antivirus to scan it on release. On these machines that scan
;  errors out, so Edge blocks the file with "Virus scan failed".
;
;  Fix: declare the app a LOCAL INTRANET site (zone 1). Intranet downloads are
;  not marked "from the Internet", so the failing scan never runs. HTTPS does
;  NOT fix this — the security ZONE is what matters.
;
;  This is the machine-wide (all users) equivalent of the GPO
;  "Site to Zone Assignment List" set to zone 1 (Local Intranet).
;  Deploy via Group Policy Preferences, SCCM/Intune, or import on each PC.
; ============================================================================

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Internet Settings\ZoneMapKey]
"http://saudization.sharbatlyfruit.com"="1"
"http://saudization"="1"
"http://192.168.3.17"="1"
